WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.370
In 1989, water in England and Wales
was sold to private companies.

2
00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:08.610
In Scotland, water stayed publicly owned.

3
00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:13.860
Yet either way, each area is still
served by a single network of pipes.

4
00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.210
Why might it make sense
for only one company

5
00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:18.310
to lay the pipes in a city?

6
00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:21.660
In this mission, you'll draw
the natural monopoly diagram,

7
00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.850
with three very different
prices it could charge.

8
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:27.020
Then you'll play the regulator.

9
00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:29.100
You'll set a price cap in a graph lab

10
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.280
and see how the firm responds.

11
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.770
Your mission: explain when
one network makes sense,

12
00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.680
and how to stop it overcharging.
